on\": \"Base document's heading chosen.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b21\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Four rules, given in the order they should be applied.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a21 version used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b22\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Honour the header every time.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Carried in merged rule 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b23\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Content in merged rule 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b24\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic with information the caller does not have, and it does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"reason\": \"503 path covered in rule 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b25\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A wait derived client-side is a guess about a counter it cannot see,\",\n      \"reason\": \"Covered in rule 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b26\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"and there is no case where a guess is better than the gateway's calculation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Covered in rule 1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b27\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Retry only what is safe to retry.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Core rule carried in rule 2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b28\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A 200 needs nothing, a 429 needs the stated wait, a 500 can be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 means the platform itself is overloaded.\",\n      \"reason\": \"b28 wording clearer than a27; used in rule 2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b29\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A client that folds all non-success responses into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a29 version used with minor rewording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b30\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A client that folds all non-success responses into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Behaviour explanation carries the prevention goal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b31\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A batch credential is allowed 1000 requests in a window, which is 50 times the default and is measured over exactly the same window, not a separate counting scheme.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Combined with a32 to include both 1000 spec and window detail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b32\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A client written for one tier needs no change at all to run against the other.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Carried in rule 3.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b33\",\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same as a34.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b34\",\n      \"disposition\": \"reconciled\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Log every refusal seen. [...] Keep the log for at least a week.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Weekly retention requirement from b34 added to a35.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b35\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused cannot argue for a larger cap, and nobody at the platform team will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a36 wording used; 'can't' changed to 'cannot'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b36\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused cannot argue for a larger cap, and nobody at the platform team will assemble that argument on its behalf.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Importance of counts implied in rule 4.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b37\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"## Other refusals and their codes\",\n      \"reason\": \"Base document's heading chosen.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b38\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three separate reasons, and only one of them is a cap.\",\n      \"reason\": \"b38 wording clearer; used over a40.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b39\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Implication carried in discussion of three reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b40\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a41 version used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b41\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The distinction matters critically to a retry loop.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a43 version reworded and used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b42\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Carried in a44 rewording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b43\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Outage misattribution idea carried in a44.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b44\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all, which is the outcome everyone prefers.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a50 version used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b45\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all, which is the outcome everyone prefers.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Cheapest fix idea carried in a50.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b46\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"A cap can be raised, but not without measurement behind the request.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a47 version used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b47\",\n      \"disposition\": \"superseded\",\n      \"replacement\": \"Bring a week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\n      \"reason\": \"a48 version used.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b48\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"replacement\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty; a burst is cheaper to smooth than to serve at its peak.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Smooth vs bursty evaluation carried in a49.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b49\",\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"replacement\": \"a burst is cheaper to smooth than to serve at its peak\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same fact as a49.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"segment\": \"b50\",\n      \"disposition\": \"subsumed\",\n      \"rep